implementationPlan.description:
Tests, one file: moe-jetbrains/src/test/kotlin/com/moe/util/RuntimeSelectionPolicyTest.kt.
- Change no existing row. That includes 526a2080's N5-N6 and S7-S8, its reopen's LEGACY stop rows, and 1c2bfeca's subst rows. Use the next free N and S numbers.
- Both new methods start with `assumeTrue("Windows path forms", RuntimeSelectionPolicy.windowsHost)`. They must RUN on the Windows verification host.
- Write runtime paths as Kotlin literals with doubled backslashes.

Helper nonLocalBases(project: File): List<String>, placed next to share() and nonLocalSpellings(). Let real = realFile(project).path (`X:\rest`) and s = share("localhost", project). Return listOfNotNull of:
- s;
- share("127.0.0.1", project);
- s.replace('\\', '/'), which is IntelliJ's system-independent basePath, `//localhost/X$/rest`;
- `\\wsl$\moe-no-such-distro\proj`;
- `\\wsl.localhost\moe-no-such-distro\proj`;
- `\\localhost\moe-no-such-share$\proj`, a missing share;
- real.substring(2), the rooted form `\rest`;
- real.substring(0, 2) + real.substring(3), the drive-relative form `X:rest`;
- volumeSpelling(project), which is `\\.\Volume{GUID}\rest` (local, no network) or null.
Its KDoc says the rule must never look any of these up.

N row, isOutsideProject.
Setup:
- project = newFolder("project"), with bin/ created;
- outside = newFolder("outside");
- store = ProtectedStateStore(temporaryFolder.root.toPath().resolve("system/moe/protected-state"));
- untouched = { throw AssertionError("looked up $it") }. It is an Error, so the catches cannot swallow it.
Assertions:
- For every base, and every path in [project.path, File(project,"bin").path, File(project,"missing").path, outside.path], assertFalse both with resolve = untouched (no candidate lookup) and with the default lookup. The outside folder is refused too, because nothing is provably outside such a base.
- For every base, assertFalse(store.usableFor(base)). Add a comment that this is an accepted cost: that project's protected state stays session-only.
- Controls through the drive path: isOutsideProject(bin, project.path) is false, outside.path is true, and store.usableFor(project.path) is true.

S row, selection and spawn.
Setup:
- (project, root, node) = protectedFixture();
- planted = File(project, "node"), containing "planted";
- sandbox = installedLayout(File(project, "build/idea-sandbox/plugins/moe-jetbrains"));
- volumeBase = volumeSpelling(project), guarded by assumeTrue("no volume GUID path on this host", volumeBase != null), as S8 does;
- reason = "the project directory is not a plain local Windows path".
For every base:
- assertEquals(reason, assertRejected(…)) for installedExecutable(planted.path, base), installedExecutable(node.path, base), installedArtifact(sandbox, "daemon/index.js", base) and installedArtifact(root, "daemon/index.js", base). The in-project pair is DoD 1. The outside pair proves that the base check refuses, not identity.
- Set env PATH to node.parentFile.path, project.path and File(project,"bin").path. Call supervisorFor(project, { null }, { null }).protectedDaemonEnvironment(env, base), then assertEquals(mapOf("PATH" to ""), env).
Spawn, through volumeBase (local, so no SMB). Let message = "Protected execution profile: $reason. Project and PATH copies of the Moe daemon are not used." For supervisorFor(File(volumeBase), { root }, { node.path }, started = started, statuses = statuses):
- ensureDaemonRunning() is false;
- started is empty;
- statuses == listOf(false to message);
- selectionRefusal() == message;
- stopCommandOrNull(volumeBase) is null.
LEGACY keeps today's stop selection:
- supervisorFor(File(volumeBase), { root }, { node.path }, profile = { RuntimeProfile.LEGACY }).stopCommandOrNull(volumeBase) equals listOf(realFile(node).path, realFile(File(root, "daemon/index.js")).path, "stop", "--project", volumeBase).
- This relies on 526a2080's reopen routing, where the switch is off under LEGACY. If it landed another way, assert the same outcome through whatever landed.
Control: installedExecutable(node.path, project.path) is Accepted(realFile(node)).

RED, then GREEN, recorded in the step note, under the jetbrains-gradle lease:
- Temporarily disable both base checks by forcing their condition to false.
- Run cmd.exe /d /c "set GRADLE_OPTS=-Xmx512m&& cd /d D:\projexts\moes\moe-jetbrains && .\gradlew.bat test --rerun --tests com.moe.util.RuntimeSelectionPolicyTest".
- Both new rows must fail. N fails through the untouched lookup or a true outside answer; S fails through an accepted outside node.
- Restore the checks and rerun: both rows pass.

